  "answer": "Project Zenith is a significant initiative that has seen various developments and milestones. The project received a major budget approval of $2M from the executive board, though a later update indicated an adjusted budget of $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and ensure the integration of real-time analytics. The team has expanded to include experts in machine learning and cloud computing, and a training budget of $15,000 was approved for specialized coding and management training. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase, the testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, and the completion of the testing phase, which was celebrated on October 10th. The project is now moving into the development phase under the guidance of lead developer Omar Jensen, with upcoming focus on user interface enhancements and stakeholder feedback submission by the end of November."
